.TH "WEBVTT" "1" "Oct 17, 2026" "0.5.1" "webvtt-py"
.SH NAME
webvtt \- segment WebVTT captions for HLS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
webvtt segment PATH \-o OUTPUT [\-d NUMBER] [\-m NUMBER]
webvtt \-h
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBwebvtt\fP segments a WebVTT caption file for \X'tty: link https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-pantos-hls-rfc8216bis'\fI\%HTTP Live Streaming\fP\X'tty: link' (HLS).
.sp
The captions in \fBPATH\fP are split into segments of a target duration. Each
segment is written to \fBOUTPUT\fP as \fBfileSequenceN.webvtt\fP, where \fBN\fP is
the segment index starting at 0, along with a playlist named
\fBprog_index.m3u8\fP that lists all the segments.
.sp
A caption whose time span crosses a segment boundary is included in every
segment it overlaps, so players display it regardless of which segment they
load.
.sp
Every segment starts with an \fBX\-TIMESTAMP\-MAP\fP header that maps the local
caption time \fB00:00:00.000\fP to an MPEG\-TS presentation timestamp, so the
captions are kept in sync with the video stream.
.SH COMMANDS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBsegment\fP
Segment the WebVTT file at \fBPATH\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB\-o OUTPUT\fP, \fB\-\-output OUTPUT\fP
Directory where the segments and playlist are written. It is created if
it does not exist. Existing files with the same names are overwritten.
Required.
.TP
.B \fB\-d NUMBER\fP, \fB\-\-target\-duration NUMBER\fP
Target duration of each segment in seconds. Also used for the
\fB#EXT\-X\-TARGETDURATION\fP and \fB#EXTINF\fP values of the playlist.
Default: \fB10\fP\&.
.TP
.B \fB\-m NUMBER\fP, \fB\-\-mpegts NUMBER\fP
MPEG\-TS value written to the \fBX\-TIMESTAMP\-MAP\fP header of each segment.
Default: \fB900000\fP (10 seconds at the 90 kHz MPEG\-TS clock).
.TP
.B \fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
Show the help message and exit.
.UNINDENT
.SH EXIT STATUS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB0\fP
The file was segmented successfully.
.TP
.B \fB1\fP
The input file could not be read or is not a valid WebVTT file, or the
output directory could not be written. An error message is printed to
standard error, for example:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
webvtt: error: captions.vtt: not a valid WebVTT file
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B \fB2\fP
Invalid command line arguments.
.UNINDENT
.SH EXAMPLE
.sp
Given \fBcaptions.vtt\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 \-\-> 00:00:04.000
Hello and welcome.

00:00:06.000 \-\-> 00:00:12.000
This caption spans two segments.

00:00:14.500 \-\-> 00:00:18.000
Thanks for watching!
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Segment it into 10 second segments:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
$ webvtt segment captions.vtt \-\-output out
$ ls out
fileSequence0.webvtt  fileSequence1.webvtt  prog_index.m3u8
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBout/prog_index.m3u8\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
#EXTM3U
#EXT\-X\-TARGETDURATION:10
#EXT\-X\-VERSION:3
#EXT\-X\-PLAYLIST\-TYPE:VOD
#EXTINF:10.00000,
fileSequence0.webvtt
#EXTINF:10.00000,
fileSequence1.webvtt
#EXT\-X\-ENDLIST
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBout/fileSequence0.webvtt\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
WEBVTT
X\-TIMESTAMP\-MAP=MPEGTS:900000,LOCAL:00:00:00.000

00:00:01.000 \-\-> 00:00:04.000
Hello and welcome.

00:00:06.000 \-\-> 00:00:12.000
This caption spans two segments.
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBout/fileSequence1.webvtt\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
WEBVTT
X\-TIMESTAMP\-MAP=MPEGTS:900000,LOCAL:00:00:00.000

00:00:06.000 \-\-> 00:00:12.000
This caption spans two segments.

00:00:14.500 \-\-> 00:00:18.000
Thanks for watching!
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Use 6 second segments and a different MPEG\-TS value:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
$ webvtt segment captions.vtt \-o out \-d 6 \-m 0
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH SEE ALSO
.sp
The same segmentation is available from Python with \fBwebvtt.segment()\fP\&.
